e_start":"011","journal_title":"JHEP"},"authors":[{"full_name":"Ghosh, A."},{"full_name":"Kundu, N."},{"full_name":"Raju, S."},{"full_name":"Trivedi, S.P."}]},"curated_relation":false,"record":{"$ref":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1276324"}}],"number_of_pages":62,"legacy_creation_date":"2015-03-30","preprint_date":"2015-03-27","author_count":2,"public_notes":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"49+12 pages. 13 figures"}],"earliest_date":"2015-03-27","facet_author_name":["999108_Juan M. Maldacena","1018121_Nima Arkani-Hamed"],"core":true,"license":[{"imposing":"arXiv","url":"http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/"}],"_oai":{"sets":["Literature"],"id":"oai:inspirehep.net:1356707","updated":"2023-03-07T04:09:42.586163"},"arxiv_eprints":[{"categories":["hep-th","astro-ph.CO","hep-ph"],"value":"1503.08043"}],"referenced_authors_bais":["A.Aravind.1","Da.Ping.Du.1","Marcello.A.Musso.1","Ru.Keng.Su.1","D.Krotov.1","N.Dalal.1","S.Deser.1","G.Shiu.1","A.J.Tolley.1","S.Garcia.Saenz.1","Jared.Daniel.Kaplan.1","Teruaki.Suyama.1","Bruce.Allen.1","T.Garidi.2","B.C.van.Rees.1","D.Huterer.1","C.de.Rham.1","Eva.Silverstein.1","S.Yokoyama.1","A.Lupsasca.1","E.H.Joung.1","K.Enqvist.1","A.Strominger.1","Min.Xin.Huang.1","K.M.Smith.1","A.L.Fitzpatrick.1","V.Pasquier.1","A.Maloney.1","A.Slosar.1","Licia.Verde.1","A.Loeb.1","A.Westphal.1","L.McAllister.1","Bin.Wang.1","Dionysios.Anninos.1","J.Bros.5","Shirley.Ho.1","Daniel.R.Green.1","A.Matusis.1","Ashish.Shukla.1","L.Senatore.1","S.P.Trivedi.1","S.Ferraro.1","D.M.Marolf.1","Masahide.Yamaguchi.1","Ian.A.Morrison.1","Sabino.Matarrese.1","K.Hinterbichler.1","A.Rajaraman.1","I.R.Klebanov.1","Yi.Wang.3","D.L.Jafferis.1","Dileep.P.Jatkar.1","Suvrat.Raju.1","D.Yokoyama.1","Edward.Witten.1","J.Norena.1","S.D.Mathur.1","L.Leblond.1","Juan.M.Maldacena.1","C.R.Nappi.1","S.R.Behbahani.1","Rachel.A.Rosen.1","A.Riotto.1","Tomo.Takahashi.1","S.Paban.1","A.Higuchi.1","Paul.L.McFadden.1","Thomas.E.Hartman.1","Henri.Epstein.1","U.Moschella.1","S.S.Gubser.1","V.Gurarie.1","C.T.Byrnes.1","A.A.Kehagias.1","M.Zaldarriaga.1","N.I.Usyukina.1","Christopher.M.Hirata.1","A.I.Davydychev.1","Nikhil.Padmanabhan.1","Olivier.P.Dore.1","K.Skenderis.1","A.Bzowski.1","A.M.Polyakov.1","M.Taronna.1","D.Lopez.Nacir.1","Tarek.Anous.1","D.Langlois.1","Toshifumi.Noumi.1","D.Lorshbough.1","Archisman.Ghosh.1","Joao.Penedones.1","A.Shirokov.1","Louise.A.Dolan.1","Mikhail.A.Vasiliev.1","Rafael.A.Porto.1","V.Assassi.1","Guido.DAmico.1","Paolo.Creminelli.1","N.Kundu.2","E.Pajer.1","Andrew.K.Waldron.1","R.I.Nepomechie.1","E.Mottola.1","Fabian.Schmidt.1","S.Kachru.1","Xingang.Chen.1","R.Holman.1","D.Wands.1","V.Lysov.1","R.Flauger.1","Gim.Seng.Ng.1","D.Z.Freedman.1","M.Gaudin.1","L.Rastelli.1","Wen.liang.Li.1","G.Konstantinidis.1","Daniel.Baumann.1","Matthew.Lewandowski.1","Uros.Seljak.1"],"figures":[{"filename":"SqueezedIntro.png","caption":"(a) The three momenta of the three point function form a closed triangle. In the squeezed limit, one of the sides, $k_{\\rm long}$, is much smaller than the other two, $k_{\\rm short}$. (b) In this limit we can also define the angle $\\gamma$ between the short and long mode momentum vectors. (c) In position space we have two insertions at a short distance from each other, associated to $k_{\\rm short}$ and one at a longer distance, $k_{\\rm long}$. We are interested in considering the effects of massive fields, $\\sigma$, that can decay into pairs of inflatons. In an inflationary background we can replace an inflaton fluctuation by the classical $\\dot \\phi_0$ background, so that we get a contribution to the three point function.","source":"arxiv","key":"c4adc68379dd7feb704dca66591cc829","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/c4adc68379dd7feb704dca66591cc829"},{"filename":"TwoThreeFour.png","caption":"(a) Two point function of massive fields (b) Three point functions of two massless fields and a massive field. (c) Four point function of massless fields with an exchange of a massive field. We can view this diagram as the amplitude to create a pair of massive fields which then decay into inflatons. (d) Contributions from Higgs field exchange, or the exchange of any other gauge non-invariant field.","source":"arxiv","key":"21058c53bea138b060b34e7a48a8e4fb","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/21058c53bea138b060b34e7a48a8e4fb"},{"filename":"FlatSpaceLimit.png","caption":"The singularity at $k_t\\to 0$ arises when the whole diagram occurs at very early times. This translates into very short distances where we can make the flat space and high energy approximation, obtaining \\nref{FlatLi}.","source":"arxiv","key":"71b5eba906f0664db3c548cec3be5a30","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/71b5eba906f0664db3c548cec3be5a30"},{"filename":"SpinCorrelation.png","caption":"(a) We see a pair of created particles that approach a given comoving points at late time in de-Sitter. There is a subgroup of the conformal group that preserves this two points. These include transformations which act as rotations around each of the two points as indicated. (b) If two points are separated along the direction $3$, then the spins of the physical particles in directions, say $J_{23}$ are the same. So the two particles would be spinning as shown. The spins in the direction $J_{12}$ are opposite.","source":"arxiv","key":"e5217332cf37cb0ecb8027011a27961d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/e5217332cf37cb0ecb8027011a27961d"},{"filename":"CollapsedTriangle.png","caption":"(a) Generic configuration of momenta for the three point function. (b) Nearly ``collapsed triangle'' configuration with $k_3 \\sim k_1 + k_2 $.","source":"arxiv","key":"790f9f10905d9ed0f657996d5e5091f1","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/790f9f10905d9ed0f657996d5e5091f1"},{"filename":"FourDiagrams.png","caption":"Diagrams for the computation of the four point function. (a) Diagram for the $\\varphi^4$ theory. (b) One of the diagrams for the $\\varphi^3$ theory. There are two other diagrams that arise by permuting the external labels.","source":"arxiv","key":"2b2826f014cb47c57d5dd7d908f043a1","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/2b2826f014cb47c57d5dd7d908f043a1"},{"filename":"OPELimit.png","caption":"Kinematic configuration in the Operator Product Expansion limit or OPE limit. (a) In momentum space the momentum $\\vec k_I = \\vec k_1 + \\vec k_2$ is much smaller than the rest. (b) In position space, points form two pairs with the two pairs far from each other. Similar limits for higher point functions when a partial sum of the momenta is zero.","source":"arxiv","key":"a6aa11fb76861a9da0d235e27111f23d","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/a6aa11fb76861a9da0d235e27111f23d"},{"filename":"stuDiagrams.png","caption":"Diagrams containing the exchange of a massive field. We consider external lines which are massless, $\\xi$, or conformally coupled scalars $\\varphi$. The $s$ diagram is the only one that can contribute non-analytic terms in the small $\\vec k_I = \\vec k_1 + \\vec k_2$ expansion.","source":"arxiv","key":"04eb2a2838a816cd6c7eb4741a579752","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/04eb2a2838a816cd6c7eb4741a579752"},{"filename":"Angles.png","caption":"Definition of the angles that enter into the answer. $\\gamma$ is the angle between $\\hat k_1$ and $\\hat k_3$. $\\psi - \\psi'$ is the angle between the projections of $\\hat k_1 $ and $\\hat k_3$ onto the plane perpendicular to $\\hat k_I$. Finally, $\\theta$ and $\\theta'$ are the angles between $\\hat k_I$ and $\\hat k_1$, $ \\hat k_3$ respectively.","source":"arxiv","key":"f696c6dc42aa45de7cb976b23b4454ab","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/f696c6dc42aa45de7cb976b23b4454ab"},{"filename":"ThreeInflation.png","caption":"Contribution to an inflationary three point function from an intermediate massive particle. The blue line with a cross is an insertion of $\\dot \\phi_0$ which is the homogeneous time derivative of the inflaton.","source":"arxiv","key":"a7e16598e06cd00550f24381f6261f90","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/a7e16598e06cd00550f24381f6261f90"},{"filename":"MuOne.png","caption":"These are plots of the function $J(\\mu, {k_3 \\over k_1} )$. The left side corresponds to $\\mu =1$, the right one to $\\mu =3$. The vertical axis displays the numerical value of $J$. The horizontal axis shows $\\log_{10} ({k_1\\over k_3} )$ which is the number of decades separating $k_1$ and $k_3$.","source":"arxiv","key":"d256052b6a958d9d1803d3c1c2c559b3","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/d256052b6a958d9d1803d3c1c2c559b3"},{"filename":"ThreeSqueezed.png","caption":"(a) Squeezed momentum contribution where $k_3 \\ll k_1 , ~k_2$. Massive fields with spin give rise to a dependence on the angle $\\theta$ between the vectors $\\vec k_3$ and $\\vec k_1 \\sim - k_2$. (b) In position space, the non analytic terms in $k_3$ give rise to correlators at long distances in position space $|x_{3,2}|, ~|x_{31}| \\gg |x_{12}| $.","source":"arxiv","key":"8ee21f1722973ac384bfc3e44bee2259","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/8ee21f1722973ac384bfc3e44bee2259"},{"filename":"LoopDiagram.png","caption":"(a)  Example of a one loop diagram arising from the coupling between the inflaton and the Higgs field $\\int (\\nabla \\phi)^2 h^\\dagger h $. (b) Example of a diagram where we have a coupling to a general four dimensional operator $\\int (\\nabla \\phi)^2 {\\cal O}^{(4)}$ and we decompose the four dimensional operator in terms of three dimensional operators with definite three dimensional conformal dimensions. The correlator in the OPE regime is governed by these dimensions. (c) When we go to an inflationary background we can also compute contributions to the three point function. (d) Loop correction to the two point function of a massive field due to a cubic self interaction.","source":"arxiv","key":"ab30c3f25df16f978746494d531c6dde","url":"https://inspirehep.net/files/ab30c3f25df16f978746494d531c6dde"}],"legacy_version":"20190305205443.0","inspire_categories":[{"term":"Theory-HEP"},{"term":"Astrophysics"},{"term":"Phenomenology-HEP"}],"urls":[{"description":"Symmetry Magazine article","value":"http://www.symmetrymagazine.org/article/august-2015/looking-for-strings-inside-inflation"}],"first_author":{"affiliations_identifiers":[{"schema":"ROR","value":"https://ror.org/00f809463"}],"full_name":"Arkani-Hamed, Nima","ids":[{"schema":"ORCID","value":"0009-0005-2750-3999"},{"schema":"INSPIRE BAI","value":"Nima.Arkani.Hamed.1"}],"last_name":"Arkani-Hamed","first_name":"Nima","recid":1018121},"control_number":1356707,"document_type":["article"],"texkeys":["Arkani-Hamed:2015bza"],"abstracts":[{"source":"arXiv","value":"We study the imprint of new particles on the primordial cosmological fluctuations. New particles with masses comparable to the Hubble scale produce a distinctive signature on the non-gaussianities. This feature arises in the squeezed limit of the correlation functions of primordial fluctuations. It consists of particular power law, or oscillatory, behavior that contains information about the masses of new particles. There is an angular dependence that gives information about the spin. We also have a relative phase that crucially depends on the quantum mechanical nature of the fluctuations and can be viewed as arising from the interference between two processes. While some of these features were noted before in the context of specific inflationary scenarios, here we give a general description emphasizing the role of symmetries in determining the final result.","abstract_source_suggest":{"input":"arXiv"}}],"primary_arxiv_category":["hep-th"],"titles":[{"source":"arXiv","title":"Cosmological Collider Physics"}],"curated":true},"links":{"bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1356707?format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1356707?format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1356707?format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1356707?format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1356707?format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/1356707?format=cv","citations":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A1356707"}}],"total":1},"links":{"self":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Arkani-Hamed%3A2015bza&size=10&page=1","bibtex":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Arkani-Hamed%3A2015bza&size=10&page=1&format=bibtex","latex-eu":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Arkani-Hamed%3A2015bza&size=10&page=1&format=latex-eu","latex-us":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Arkani-Hamed%3A2015bza&size=10&page=1&format=latex-us","json":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Arkani-Hamed%3A2015bza&size=10&page=1&format=json","json-expanded":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Arkani-Hamed%3A2015bza&size=10&page=1&format=json-expanded","cv":"https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=texkey%20Arkani-Hamed%3A2015bza&size=10&page=1&format=cv"}}